Exercise: sa-users-review (chapter 6 lab)

Work on serverb, with sudo or as root.

Group
 1. operators, with GID 35000.

Accounts
 2. opsadmin: UID 3101, a member of operators (supplementary), comment
    "Operations Admin". Its password is Temp-Pass-2026, which opsadmin must
    change at the first login. Its password must change at least every 60
    days, with 10 days of warning.
 3. auditor: comment "Security Auditor", not in operators. Set its password
    to Audit-Pass-2026, then lock it. The account expires on 2026-12-31.
 4. backup: a service account with UID 3200, primary group operators, and
    the login shell /sbin/nologin.

Root access
 5. Members of operators may run /usr/bin/systemctl, with any arguments, as
    any user, after entering their own password. Put the rule in
    /etc/sudoers.d/operators, mode 440, and nothing else in that file.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-users-review
